WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.970
The reality-warping nature of Crisis on Infinite
Earths brings up loads of questions about

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.720
not only the Arrowverse, but the worlds beyond
the CW's series.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.090
Some of these questions may be answered in
the coming months, and some may never be answered

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:13.720
at all.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.920
The first three parts of Crisis bring some
incredible cameos, but the one that lit the

00:00:18.929 --> 00:00:24.489
internet on fire was saved for Part 4 Ezra
Miller, who appears as the Flash in 2017's

00:00:24.489 --> 00:00:29.259
Justice League, comes face-to-face with Grant
Gustin's CW version of the character as the

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.280
latter is traveling through the Speed Force.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.820
Neither of them have any idea of how the meeting
is possible, and the movie Flash in particular

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.340
seems completely oblivious, though the pair
get a somewhat awkward moment appreciating

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.440
each others' costumes.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.160
As the TV Flash says, this shouldn't be able
to happen.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.980
At this point the multiverse has been annihilated
by the anti-matter wave.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.960
So if the DCEU films are meant to take place
in the same multiverse as the Arrowverse,

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.260
the movie Flash should be wiped out along
with the rest of that Earth's heroes.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.420
"You've been gone for months.”

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.880
“What are you talking about ....I just left
two seconds ago."

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.370
One possible explanation is that time in the
Speed Force doesn't work the same as it does

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:05.860
on Earth.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.120
We've already seen this is the case in previous
seasons of The Flash.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.610
So, as confusing as it may seem, it could
be the movie Flash entered the Speed Force

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:18.140
before the multiverse's death and the Force's
strange relationship with time is allowing

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.000
him to meet the TV Flash after the end of
all things.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.780
One of the coolest things about Crisis on
Infinite Earths is the reprisal of Brandon

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.360
Routh in the role of Superman.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.640
In earlier chapters of Crisis he plays the
Superman of Earth-96, who is largely based

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.140
on the 1996 miniseries Kingdom Come.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.260
Routh's Earth-96 Superman has earned some
gray hairs and his costume insignia incorporates

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.920
the color black something uncommon for the
character outside of Kingdom Come.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.700
He's killed by Lex Luthor at the end of Crisis
Part 3, but by the end of the event we learn

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.820
the restoration of the multiverse has resurrected
the hero.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:57.270
During the resolution of Crisis Part 5, we
see snapshots of other corners of the multiverse,

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:58.590
including Earth-96.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.700
We find a smiling Superman flying in orbit
over the Earth.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.900
Interestingly, his costume has changed.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.510
The black of his trademark insignia has been
replaced with yellow, and overall his costume

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:13.040
looks much more like the one Routh wore in
2006's Superman Returns.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:17.160
We don't know if the change is a conscious
choice on Superman's part or a result of the

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.540
changes in the multiverse.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.300
One possibility is that it's meant to signify
the character has found some peace.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:26.660
When he's asked about the black in the costume
earlier in Crisis, he says it symbolizes that

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.870
there's hope even in the darkest of times.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.380
Perhaps this version of the Man of Steel no
longer finds himself in the darkest of times,

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.560
and decided to let it show.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:40.020
Oliver Queen dies a second time at the end
of Crisis Part 4, and this one might just

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:40.520
stick.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:45.180
With the powers of the Spectre, Queen dies
battling the Anti-Monitor and helping to restore

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:45.920
the multiverse.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.520
His sacrifice is lamented by all the heroes
in Part 5, and the President of the United

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.820
States calls for a moment of silence in honor
of his deeds.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.760
Even if we accept this is, finally, the end
of a character who has already died and come

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.530
back multiple times in the history of the
Arrowverse, we're left with the question of

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.930
what happened to Spectre.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:05.840
We don't know a lot about the Arrowverse's
version of the Spectre.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:11.060
He's introduced in Crisis Part 3 when James
Corrigan approaches Oliver Queen in Purgatory

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:16.140
about acting as the spirit's new host, and
by Part 4 Oliver has assumed his new role.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.700
In the comics, the Spectre is the physical
embodiment of the wrath of God and one of

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.940
the most powerful superheroes of DC.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:27.880
If the Spectre of the CW is similar to that
of the comics, the death of Oliver Queen would

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:32.290
likely not mean the death of the Spectre,
but instead the spirit would need a new host.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.950
So, did the Spectre find one?

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.920
Did it go back to James Corrigan?

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:40.480
Or is it possible Oliver isn't dead, and will
continue to act as the Spectre in the shadows?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.660
Crisis Part 3 introduces us to Ryan Choi,
the Paragon of Humanity.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.380
He's one of the only Paragons to be introduced
in Crisis, at least as far as the Arrowverse

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:50.880
is concerned.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.540
But DC Comics readers are more familiar with
the name.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:59.180
Choi famously replaces Ray Palmer as the shrinking
hero Atom in the All-New Atom comic series.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:04.540
While Choi's solo series didn't last, he remained
a hero in the DC universe, most recently being

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:09.020
recruited into an eccentric Justice League
of America lineup that included the reformed

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.140
villain Killer Frost and the alien bounty
hunter Lobo.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:16.240
His appearance naturally had fans wondering
if he'd be joining the super-powered club

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:20.969
by the end of Crisis, but Part 5 concludes
without Choi obtaining any shrinking powers

00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:23.360
or a suit of armor similar to Ray Palmer's.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.620
"This definitely makes me question again why
I'm here."

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:30.000
But that doesn't mean Choi couldn't play a
larger role in the Arrowverse's future, and

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.140
possibly as another version of the Atom.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.920
As soon as we meet him in Crisis, he makes
it clear he's familiar with Ray Palmer's scientific

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:40.719
breakthroughs, and it's Choi who comes up
with the idea of making a device that will

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:44.220
neutralize the Anti-Monitor by making him
shrink infinitely.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.340
Whether or not this is a sign of things to
come, only time will tell.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:53.120
Crisis Part 5 ends with the multiverse restored,
but not exactly as it used to be.

00:04:53.139 --> 00:04:58.409
The various heroes of the different CW Arrowverse
series existed on a few separate Earths before

00:04:58.409 --> 00:05:01.280
Crisis, but they now share the same world
Earth Prime.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.340
"It's normal to see us together?"

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.160
"Well, normally you'd also have Green Arrow
and a Legend or two."

00:05:08.169 --> 00:05:10.139
But what about the rest of the multiverse?

00:05:10.139 --> 00:05:14.800
We don't revisit Earth-89, where we saw Robert
Wuhl reprise the role of intrepid Batman-hunting

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.260
reporter Alexander Knox.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:19.280
We don't get another visit with the Robin
of Earth-66.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.320
And we don't see the fate of Earth-167, where
the events of Smallville take place.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:27.729
It's likely we won't see most of those worlds
again in the Arrowverse series, and really,

00:05:27.729 --> 00:05:28.360
that's okay.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:32.040
What could have an impact on the Arrowverse
going forward are some of the alternate Earths

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.340
we visited before Crisis.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:38.340
For example, there's Earth-X, where the CW
heroes put a dent in the Nazi ruling faction

00:05:38.349 --> 00:05:43.770
in the 2017 crossover Crisis on Earth-X - and
made it easier for The Ray to go back home

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:44.980
and take them out for good.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.370
Or what about Earth-90, which was destroyed
as part of the 2018 crossover Elseworlds?

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.940
Was the Barry Allen of the '90s Flash show
resurrected as part of the multiverse's restoration?

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:01.840
In Crisis Part 3, Constantine, Diggle, and
Mia travel to Earth-666 as part of their quest

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.240
to resurrect Oliver Queen.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.240
There, we meet Tom Ellis' Lucifer Morningstar
from the series Lucifer.

00:06:07.249 --> 00:06:11.779
From their back and forth it's clear Lucifer
and Constantine have had dealings before,

00:06:11.779 --> 00:06:15.630
and in particular Lucifer says something which
has had fans of the Arrowverse and Lucifer

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:16.860
scratching their heads.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.200
"Okay, I'm only doing this because I owe you
for Maze."

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:24.620
Maze, or Mazikeen, is a regular character
on Lucifer played by Lesley-Ann Brandt.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:27.660
She's a demon who used to be the most feared
torturer in all of Hell.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:32.440
But by the end of Part 5 we get no indication
of exactly what Constantine did for Maze and

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:32.940
Lucifer.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:37.740
Not even Lucifer showrunners Joe Henderson
and Ildy Modrovich know what the former monarch

00:06:37.749 --> 00:06:39.119
of Hell was talking about.

00:06:39.119 --> 00:06:42.990
They told EW the line was as much a surprise
to them as it was to the fans.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:46.999
If the issue is ever to be addressed on Lucifer,
it will have to be in its upcoming fifth and

00:06:46.999 --> 00:06:48.020
final season.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:52.280
Otherwise, Lucifer and/or Maze will have to
make one more visit to the Arrowverse, or

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.280
fans will be left to wonder.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:58.599
Early in Part 5 of Crisis, we learn one of
the biggest changes in the restored multiverse

00:06:58.599 --> 00:07:02.789
is that only Supergirl and the other Paragons
remember Lex Luthor as being the villain we

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:03.789
all know he is.

00:07:03.789 --> 00:07:08.259
When Supergirl first awakens in the new Earth
Prime, she's late to cover Lex being awarded

00:07:08.259 --> 00:07:12.119
the Nobel Peace Prize, and we soon learn he's
somehow the head of the D.E.O.

00:07:12.119 --> 00:07:17.189
Even close allies of Supergirl, like her sister
Alex, look up to Lex as some kind of benevolent

00:07:17.189 --> 00:07:17.960
philanthropist.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.180
"He's the best guy."

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.260
No, he's not; he's a psychopathic lunatic!"

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.120
"What?"

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:27.280
The most likely answer to how this came to
be is that it was by Lex's design.

00:07:27.289 --> 00:07:31.280
Just before Oliver Queen's confrontation with
the Anti-Monitor and the formation of the

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:35.710
new multiverse, Lex reminds the other Paragons
he still has a piece of the Book of Destiny

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:40.159
which he'd previously used to kill the Superman
of Earth-96 and take his place.

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:44.279
With the remaining pieces of the Book of Destiny,
coupled with his own intellect, Lex may have

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.699
figured a way to consciously will himself
into a new role on Earth Prime.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:51.020
“So this is what being a hero feels like..
interesting...?”

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:55.819
Regardless of how he did it, Jon Cryer's been
a hit in his portrayal of one of DC's chief

00:07:55.819 --> 00:08:00.270
villains, and it's good to know Crisis is
unlikely to be the end of his time as Lex

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:00.800
Luthor.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:06.020
Toward the end of Part 5, Lois Lane drops
a bombshell and Tyler Hoechlin's Superman

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.960
seems just as surprised as the rest of us.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:12.119
Lois calls Superman as he's flying through
the clouds and tells him he needs to get to

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.200
Metropolis, saying simply, "It's the boys."

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.960
Superman dives toward the Earth, presumably
on his way home, but we never get to see these

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.140
boys for ourselves.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:24.000
The last time we left them, Superman and Lois
had one child, Jonathan.

00:08:24.009 --> 00:08:27.760
The newborn lends some much needed humor to
exposition scenes with The Monitor, as he

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:30.960
keeps interrupting the alien's portents of
doom with his crying.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.900
But somehow the restoration of the multiverse
has given Lois and Clark at least one more

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:35.400
son.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.640
This is a departure not only from the pre-Crisis
CW, but from the comics.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:44.060
Jonathan is the son of Lois and Clark in the
comics though he's the teenage Superboy and

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.680
a member of the Legion of Super-Heroes.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:51.440
"You know when I used to picture us together,
we were living on Earth, and we had two kids."

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:55.279
It's an interesting twist that's sure to cause
the pair complications down the road.

00:08:55.279 --> 00:08:59.160
We'll likely learn who these sons are, how
many there are, and whether they've inherited

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:03.190
any of their father's abilities either in
future episodes of Supergirl, or in their

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.300
own upcoming series Superman &amp; Lois.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.810
In Crisis Part 2, the heroes encounter the
earlier version of a cowboy anti-hero they've

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:14.550
had dealings with in the past Jonah Hex, played
by Johnathon Schaech.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.980
They're confronted by Hex in a mine on Earth-18
where they're looking for a Lazarus Pit to

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:20.280
resurrect Oliver Queen.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:25.420
Sara Lance and Mia fight and overpower Hex,
who as of yet doesn't have his trademark scar.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:29.450
When Jonah, restrained by Sara, refuses to
yield and give them permission to be in the

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:34.009
mine, Sara says "Guess you were going to get
this scar eventually," and cuts into his face

00:09:34.009 --> 00:09:34.560
with a knife.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:38.780
In the comics, Hex's scar comes from a fire
and it doesn't look like an injury that a

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.550
knife would cause all on its own.

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:44.300
If this is actually meant to be the event
that marks Jonah Hex for good, the fact that

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:47.320
the multiverse essentially gets a big reboot
might undo it.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:52.240
Hex doesn't appear at all after Part 2 of
the event, so as of yet we have no idea whether

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.660
or not he still has Sara to thank for his
good looks.

00:09:55.460 --> 00:10:00.720
In Crisis Part 2, Batwoman and Supergirl travel
to Earth-99 where they believe they can find

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:03.560
the Paragon of Courage that world's version
of Batman.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:07.941
Instead, they find an old, broken Bruce Wayne
who is content to let his world and the rest

00:10:07.941 --> 00:10:08.900
of the multiverse die.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:13.180
We learn at some point this version of Batman
crossed the line and killed one of his enemies,

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.580
after which killing eventually became his
default.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:17.940
He even killed his world's version of Superman.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:23.140
"Battle not with monsters, lest you become
a monster."

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:26.600
But we never learn what it was that pushed
Batman over the edge.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:30.629
We get a few dark details, but they all seem
to have happened after he went rogue.

00:10:30.629 --> 00:10:34.720
He mentions the Batwoman of Earth-99 died,
but this looks likely to have happened after

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:39.300
Batman went bad, because Bruce says his Kate
first became Batwoman because she "thought

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:43.129
she could succeed where I failed" implying
he'd already been corrupted before she even

00:10:43.129 --> 00:10:44.020
became a hero.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:47.720
His final battle with Superman would be an
unlikely source, considering he would have

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:51.600
already gone down a much darker road in order
to become Superman's target.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:55.980
If we absolutely had to guess, then it seems
a good bet it was the Joker who finally drove

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.060
the Dark Knight to cross the uncrossable line.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.980
We know the clown has brought other versions
of Batman close to the brink before.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:07.029
Still, the Bruce Wayne of Earth-99 dies without
ever mentioning specifics, so we'll probably

00:11:07.029 --> 00:11:08.400
never know for sure.

